    "storage": {
      "value": "<ac:layout><ac:layout-section ac:type=\"two_right_sidebar\"><ac:layout-cell><h2>Purpose and Benefits</h2><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">User can export reports using this configuration for any analysis. User can create filter list and save it for future use.<br style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\" /></span></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">Steps</span></h2><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">1.&nbsp;Login</span></h3><p>Login to OpenERP with admin privileges.</p><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><strong>2. Click on Purchases, Purchase Orders</strong>.</span></h3><p><br /></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">Choose Purchases and then Purchase Order from left side panel as shown in the screenshot below.</span></p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"tip\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"ffe7ba81-a545-45c8-b1af-4374e780f2e2\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"title\">Example</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\">As an example, we have added Purchase flow, similarly we can export any module report like Sales,Accounting,Warehouse</span></p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p><br /></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><ac:image ac:align=\"center\" ac:title=\"Click on Purchases then click on Purchase order\" ac:alt=\"Click on Purchases then click on Purchase order\" ac:width=\"1000\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Purchase Orders   OpenERP.png\" /></ac:image></span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><strong>Purchase Orders.</strong></span><br /></span></p><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><strong>3.</strong> Add<strong> the date filter from the Advance filter.</strong><br /></span></h3><p><br /></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><strong><ac:image ac:width=\"1000\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Advance_Date_filter_New.png\" /></ac:image><br /></strong></span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><strong>Advance Filters.</strong></span></p><h3><span><span style=\"color: rgb(0,0,0);\"><strong>3. </strong></span><strong>Click on</strong></span><strong> Reference<strong> Column &amp; Export Report</strong>.</strong></h3><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><ac:image ac:width=\"1000\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Purchase Orders   OpenERP_Export.png\" /></ac:image></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Column name &amp; Export Report .</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>4.We can add</strong> columns<strong> from the Available fields &amp; save the List for the future use.</strong></h3><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><ac:image ac:width=\"1000\"><ri:attachment ri:filename=\"Purchase Orders   OpenERP_Future_List.png\" /></ac:image></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Save Fields List</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">User can add configuration &amp; export report in any module of openerp.</p><p><br /></p></ac:layout-cell><ac:layout-cell><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"tip\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"e6921b04-2089-48cb-990e-45bb5d87af22\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"icon\">false</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"title\">On this Page</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"toc\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:macro-id=\"eddf93f6-bb0d-414a-90d5-d02ec0df0800\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"style\">none</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro></ac:layout-cell></ac:layout-section></ac:layout>",
